   "component": "CYS2 / CYS7 (thioether staple) covalent_junctions.distance_A",
   "issue": "Both cysteines are modelled only to CB (the Sgamma is absent), and the staple is recorded as CYS.CB-I1J.S (1.81/1.73 A, normal C-S). distance_A is therefore a reconstructed value for the absent Sgamma, and the original values (0.67/0.32) came from reconstructing Sgamma at an arbitrary chi1; a thiol's Sgamma hangs off CB by a freely-rotating bond, so an arbitrary chi1 can land it far from the partner (worst case ~3.3 A).",
   "fix": "Recomputed distance_A as the closest a geometrically-valid Sgamma placement (scanning chi1, ideal CB-SG 1.808 A / CA-CB-SG 114.4 deg) comes to the bonded staple sulfur: 0.10 A (CYS2->I1J.S5) and 0.16 A (CYS7->I1J.S6). This is consistent with the rigid sp2-oxygen junctions (~0.1 A) and correctly reflects that the staple sulfur occupies a valid Sgamma site. The crystal coordinates and the CB-S bond are unchanged.",
